module Main
import Bytes

-- FFI Slice 4 Task 1 coherence, REJECT: ForeignBlessedMoveOutNeedsOwned (the
-- dual, latent-use-after-move direction). `consume` is blessed with MoveOut at
-- position 0, but this signature omits `owned` on that parameter. The runtime
-- router (Task 4) acts on the BLESSED transfer list, so it would move/free the
-- buffer while the checker treated it as a still-usable borrow -- a
-- use-after-move. Rejecting here keeps surface `owned` <=> blessed MoveOut.
foreign module Sink "wok" where
  consume "consume" : Bytes -> U64 with IO

main = Sink.consume (fromList [65, 66, 67])
